{
  "version": 1,
  "_doc": [
    "C2 gate policy (judge/hooks/gate.py). Deterministic: no model calls.",
    "Render-time placeholders use the brace form and come from site.env (rendered by install.sh, or at",
    "runtime by gate.py when $JUDGE_REVIEW_DIR/gate-policy.json is absent).",
    "Run-time path variables use the bare form and are expanded by gate.py on every call:",
    "  ~  $HOME  $HERMES_HOME  $JUDGE_REVIEW_DIR  $JUDGE_DIR (the judge/ directory gate.py lives in).",
    "Each rule: id, description, kind (selects the matcher engine in gate.py), action (approve|block),",
    "plus kind-specific matcher data. approve = escalate to the human; block = refuse outright.",
    "Precedence: any block beats any approve; no hit = pass ({})."
  ],
  "hosts": {
    "backend": {
      "label": "Walter",
      "addresses": ["${BACKEND_LAN_IP}", "${BACKEND_WG_IP}"],
      "domains": [],
      "users": ["${BACKEND_SSH_USER}"],
      "aliases": []
    },
    "edge": {
      "label": "Covenant",
      "addresses": ["${EDGE_PUBLIC_IP}", "${EDGE_WG_IP}"],
      "domains": ["${SPARK_DOMAIN}"],
      "users": ["${EDGE_SSH_USER}"],
      "aliases": ["${JUDGE_SSH_ALIASES}"]
    }
  },
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "oversight-config",
      "kind": "oversight_config",
      "action": "block",
      "description": "Change to oversight settings in the Hermes config (allowlist, hooks, security, approvals, verify nudges)",
      "path": "$HERMES_HOME/config.yaml",
      "keys": ["command_allowlist", "hooks", "hooks_auto_accept", "security", "approvals", "agent.max_verify_nudges"],
      "hermes_cli_block_flags": ["--yolo", "--accept-hooks"],
      "hermes_cli_block_env": ["HERMES_ACCEPT_HOOKS", "HERMES_YOLO_MODE"],
      "hermes_cli": {
        "_doc": "`hermes` on the terminal. -h/--help anywhere before `--` passes (argparse exits first). config set/unset of an oversight key and the *_block entries block; read-only forms pass; any other config/hooks action and approve_subcommands escalate as hermes-config. config get --raw is secret-output. approvals suggest --apply blocks (writes command_allowlist). Read-only lists verified against `hermes <sub> --help` and hermes_cli/config.py (_CONFIG_SUBCOMMANDS) / hermes_cli/hooks.py (_ACTIONS).",
        "config_readonly": ["", "show", "get", "path", "env-path", "check"],
        "config_block": ["edit"],
        "hooks_readonly": ["", "list", "ls", "doctor"],
        "hooks_block": ["revoke", "remove", "rm", "approve", "accept", "allow"],
        "block_subcommands": ["import"],
        "approve_subcommands": ["setup", "migrate"]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "oversight-path",
      "kind": "oversight_path",
      "action": "block",
      "description": "Write to the agent's own oversight machinery (hook consent allowlist, hook scripts, judge/, review dir)",
      "paths": [
        "$HERMES_HOME/shell-hooks-allowlist.json",
        "$HERMES_HOME/agent-hooks/**",
        "$JUDGE_DIR/**",
        "$JUDGE_REVIEW_DIR/**"
      ],
      "except": ["$JUDGE_REVIEW_DIR/acks/**"],
      "judge_dir_markers": ["hooks/gate.py", "CONTRACT.md"]
    },
    {
      "id": "hermes-config",
      "kind": "hermes_config",
      "action": "approve",
      "description": "Edit to the Hermes config that does not touch oversight keys, or a hermes CLI action not known to be read-only (still a human decision)",
      "path": "$HERMES_HOME/config.yaml"
    },
    {
      "id": "sensitive-path",
      "kind": "sensitive_path",
      "action": "approve",
      "description": "Write to a sensitive local path (ssh config/keys, Hermes .env, spark client config, /etc)",
      "paths": ["~/.ssh/**", "$HERMES_HOME/.env", "~/.config/spark/**", "/etc/**"]
    },
    {
      "id": "remote-mutation",
      "kind": "remote_mutation",
      "action": "approve",
      "description": "Command that changes state on Walter or Covenant",
      "readonly_commands": [
        "cat", "tac", "ls", "ll", "dir", "tree", "grep", "egrep", "fgrep", "rg", "zgrep", "zcat", "bzcat", "xzcat",
        "head", "tail", "less", "more", "wc", "stat", "file", "du", "df", "free", "uptime", "uname", "whoami",
        "id", "groups", "ps", "pgrep", "pidof", "top", "ss", "netstat", "lsof", "lsblk", "blkid", "findmnt",
        "echo", "printf", "true", "false", "test", "[", "[[", "]]", "sleep", "which", "whereis", "type",
        "readlink", "realpath", "dirname", "basename", "sha256sum", "sha1sum", "sha512sum", "md5sum", "b2sum",
        "cksum", "diff", "cmp", "sort", "uniq", "cut", "tr", "column", "jq", "paste", "nl", "fold", "fmt", "seq",
        "expr", "bc", "namei", "getfacl", "lsattr", "getent", "last", "lastlog", "w", "who", "lscpu", "lspci",
        "lsusb", "lsmod", "modinfo", "nproc", "vmstat", "iostat", "mpstat", "sensors", "ping", "dig", "host",
        "nslookup", "getconf", "locale", "printenv", "systemd-analyze", "cd", "pwd", "export", "set", "unset",
        "local", "declare", "typeset", "readonly", "read", "exit", "return", ":", "shift", "break",
        "continue", "let", "wait", "iptables-save", "ip6tables-save", "apt-cache",
        "dpkg-query", "base64", "xxd", "od", "hexdump", "strings", "rev", "comm", "join", "env", "nvidia-smi"
      ],
      "readonly_subcommands": {
        "systemctl": ["", "status", "is-active", "is-enabled", "is-failed", "is-system-running", "show", "cat",
                      "list-units", "list-unit-files", "list-timers", "list-sockets", "list-dependencies",
                      "list-jobs", "get-default", "show-environment", "help"],
        "docker": ["", "ps", "logs", "inspect", "images", "top", "port", "stats", "version", "info", "events",
                   "diff", "history", "image ls", "image list", "image inspect", "image history",
                   "container ls", "container list", "container inspect", "container logs", "container top",
                   "container port", "container stats", "container diff", "network ls", "network list",
                   "network inspect", "volume ls", "volume list", "volume inspect", "system df", "system info",
                   "system events", "context ls", "context list", "context show", "context inspect",
                   "buildx ls", "plugin ls", "compose"],
        "docker compose": ["", "ps", "logs", "config", "images", "ls", "top", "version", "port", "events"],
        "ufw": ["status", "show", "version", "app"],
        "certbot": ["certificates", "plugins"],
        "apt": ["list", "show", "policy", "search", "depends", "rdepends", "showsrc"],
        "wg": ["", "show"],
        "fail2ban-client": ["status", "ping", "version", "get", "banned"],
        "timedatectl": ["", "status", "show", "list-timezones", "timesync-status", "show-timesync"],
        "hostnamectl": ["", "status", "hostname"],
        "resolvectl": ["", "status", "query", "statistics", "dns", "domain"],
        "loginctl": ["", "list-sessions", "list-users", "list-seats", "show-session", "show-user", "session-status", "user-status"],
        "git": ["status", "log", "diff", "show", "rev-parse", "ls-files", "ls-remote", "describe", "blame",
                "shortlog", "grep", "cat-file", "ls-tree", "reflog", "remote", "branch", "tag", "config"],
        "nft": ["list"]
      },
      "certbot_dry_run": "approve",
      "certbot_dry_run_note": "certbot renew --dry-run still runs --pre-hook/--post-hook (which commonly stop/start nginx) and writes logs, so it is escalated, not passed."
    },
    {
      "id": "remote-copy",
      "kind": "remote_copy",
      "action": "approve",
      "description": "File transfer TO Walter or Covenant (scp/rsync/sftp destination on the host)"
    },
    {
      "id": "remote-opaque",
      "kind": "remote_opaque",
      "action": "approve",
      "description": "Remote session whose commands the gate cannot see (interactive ssh, script piped from a local file)"
    },
    {
      "id": "public-push",
      "kind": "public_push",
      "action": "approve",
      "description": "Publishing to a remote: git push (the deck repo is PUBLIC), gh pr merge, gh repo/release mutations, gh api writes",
      "gh_mutations": {
        "pr": ["merge"],
        "repo": ["create", "delete", "edit", "rename", "archive", "unarchive", "fork", "sync", "deploy-key"],
        "release": ["create", "delete", "edit", "upload", "delete-asset"],
        "secret": ["set", "delete", "remove"],
        "variable": ["set", "delete"]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "secret-output",
      "kind": "secret_output",
      "action": "approve",
      "description": "Command or read_file that would put a secret, or any part of it, into the transcript. If this is escalated and refused, stop and report it to the human; do not reach the same file another way",
      "_doc_read_file": "read_file escalates when the path is secret-shaped by secret_names (basename) or secret_paths (full path), minus not_secret_names; every other read passes. $HERMES_HOME/config.yaml deliberately passes: it holds settings, not credentials (those live in $HERMES_HOME/.env, which escalates), the agent needs it to reason about its own setup, and Hermes's output redactor still masks key-shaped values.",
      "secret_paths": [
        "~/.config/spark/**", "$HERMES_HOME/.env", "~/.ssh/id_*", "/etc/llama-swap/api-key", "/etc/wireguard/**",
        "/etc/ssh/ssh_host_*_key", "~/.git-credentials", "~/.docker/config.json", "~/.config/gh/hosts.yml"
      ],
      "secret_names": [
        "*.key", "*.pem", ".env", "*.env", "api-key", "api_key", "apikey", "*-api-key", "*_api_key",
        "*secret*", "admin-password", "*password*", "shadow", "gshadow", "id_rsa", "id_ecdsa", "id_ed25519",
        "id_dsa", "*.p12", "*.pfx", "*.keystore", "credentials", "credentials.json", ".netrc", ".pgpass",
        "auth.json", "wg*.conf", "token", "*.token", "*-token", "*_token", "privkey*", "*.age", "*.kdbx"
      ],
      "not_secret_names": [
        "*.pub", "*.example", "*.sample", "*.tmpl", "*.template", "*.md", "*.sh", "*.py", "*.rs", "*.go",
        "*.js", "*.ts", "*.d", "*.service", "*.j2", "*.html", "*.css"
      ],
      "print_commands": [
        "cat", "tac", "less", "more", "head", "tail", "bat", "batcat", "nl", "xxd", "od", "hexdump", "strings",
        "base64", "base32", "view", "grep", "egrep", "fgrep", "rg", "zgrep", "awk", "gawk", "mawk", "sed", "diff",
        "cut", "sort", "uniq", "column", "jq", "yq", "rev", "fold", "paste", "dd"
      ],
      "safe_sinks": ["wc", "sha256sum", "sha1sum", "sha512sum", "md5sum", "b2sum", "cksum", "true", "test"],
      "secret_grep_pattern": "(?i)(api[_-]?key|secret|passw(or)?d|private[_ -]?key|bearer|master[_-]?key|auth[_-]?token|access[_-]?token)",
      "_doc_secret_grep": "#36: secret_grep_pattern is matched against the grep/rg PATTERN, which is text to match, never a path. It escalates only when what is searched may hold a secret: stdin, a remote host, an unresolved operand, a file whose name is not in not_secret_names, or a tree (grep -r, rg) that is or covers a secret path or holds a secret-shaped file (bounded walk; a tree too large to walk escalates; --include/-g globs made only of not_secret_names skip the walk). Words that occur only in grep/sed/awk patterns do not count as a secret mention for secret-output-unknown.",
      "_doc_syntax_check": "#36: bash/sh/zsh/dash/ksh -n (or -o noexec) FILE and shellcheck FILE run nothing, so FILE's contents are not analyzed; they escalate only when FILE (or a < stdin redirect) is itself secret-shaped, since syntax errors and lint output quote source lines. bash -n -c CODE is still analyzed.",
      "_doc_variables": "#27: shell variables assigned to literal values in the same command line or script (X=..., export/local/declare/readonly/typeset X=..., ~ and $HOME expanded) are substituted into later words before the path checks, including inside bash -c / eval / $(...). A copy of a secret (cp/mv/install/ln, or a captured read redirected to a file) is treated as a secret for the rest of the command. A digest of a byte-limited part of a secret (head -c/tail -c/cut -c/dd count= piped to a hash) escalates: it is brute-forceable."
    },
    {
      "id": "secret-output-unknown",
      "kind": "secret_output_unknown",
      "action": "approve",
      "description": "A printing command reads a file the gate cannot resolve (command substitution, unknown or loop variable, read, xargs/find -exec argument) in a command that names a secret path or secret-shaped file; it may print that secret",
      "_doc": "#27. Uses the secret_output lists (secret_paths, secret_names, not_secret_names, print_commands). Fires only when the same command line (or a script it runs) mentions something secret-shaped anywhere (an assignment, a glob such as ~/.config/spark/*, a find root/filter), or when a find/xargs listing walks a directory that contains a secret path; otherwise an unresolved argument passes, to avoid approval fatigue."
    }
  ]
}
